
---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Me | Shivraj Deshmukh"
  description="A little about my background, my ambitions in theoretical physics and philosophy, and the research, discipline, writing, and creative work that shape my life."
>
  <main class="about-page">
    <!-- INTRODUCTION -->
    <section class="about-hero">
      <div class="about-container">
        <div class="about-hero-grid">
          <div class="about-hero-copy">
            <span class="about-eyebrow">ABOUT ME</span>

            <h1>
              Trying to understand the universe,
              <em>and my place in it.</em>
            </h1>

            <p class="about-lead">
              I am a research student interested in theoretical physics,
              particularly the questions surrounding gravity, quantum theory,
              and the structure of the universe. But the questions that keep
              me curious extend beyond physics. They concern how we understand
              reality, what it means to learn something deeply, and how one
              might build a meaningful life around the pursuit of understanding.
            </p>

            <p class="about-hero-note">
              Research, philosophy, discipline, and a life of continued learning.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="about-identity" aria-label="A few things about me">
            <div class="identity-orbit orbit-one"></div>
            <div class="identity-orbit orbit-two"></div>
            <div class="identity-core">
              <span class="identity-symbol">∴</span>
              <span class="identity-label">Curiosity without a finish line</span>
            </div>

            <div class="identity-note identity-note-top">
              <span class="identity-dot"></span>
              <span>Understand</span>
            </div>

            <div class="identity-note identity-note-bottom">
              <span class="identity-dot"></span>
              <span>Question</span>
            </div>

            <div class="identity-caption">
              <span>AN ONGOING PROCESS</span>
              <p>Learning to ask better questions, one step at a time.</p>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>

        <div class="about-hero-footer">
          <span>THEORETICAL PHYSICS</span>
          <span>PHILOSOPHY</span>
          <span>LEARNING</span>
          <span>CREATIVE WORK</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- BACKGROUND -->
    <section class="about-section about-origin">
      <div class="about-container">
        <div class="about-section-heading">
          <span class="about-index">01 / BACKGROUND</span>
          <h2>Where I come from matters to the story.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="about-prose">
          <p>
            I come from a farming family. That is an important part of my
            background and of how I understand my own journey. My interests
            now take me into abstract questions about gravity, geometry,
            quantum theory, and the foundations of reality, but my life is
            not defined by academic work alone.
          </p>

          <p>
            I am still figuring things out, learning what I am capable of,
            and working towards a life that feels worth living. I do not see
            my background and my intellectual ambitions as competing parts
            of my identity. They belong to the same story: the story of
            someone trying to learn, grow, and make something meaningful
            out of the opportunities and time available to him.
          </p>

          <p>
            I am not writing this as a finished account of who I am. I am
            still becoming that person. What I can describe honestly is the
            direction I want to move in, the questions I want to pursue,
            and the kind of effort I want to bring to them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PHYSICS -->
    <section class="about-section about-physics">
      <div class="about-container">
        <div class="about-section-heading">
          <span class="about-index">02 / RESEARCH</span>
          <h2>The questions that draw me to physics.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="about-two-column">
          <div class="about-prose">
            <p>
              My academic interests lie in theoretical physics, especially
              quantum gravity, three-dimensional gravity, AdS/CFT, and
              high-energy physics. I am interested in the mathematical
              structures that let us describe nature, and in what those
              structures reveal about the relationship between gravity,
              quantum theory, geometry, and information.
            </p>

            <p>
              I am drawn to questions where different descriptions of
              physical reality meet. How should we understand gravity
              at the quantum level? What can lower-dimensional models
              teach us about more general gravitational systems? What does
              holography tell us about the relationship between spacetime
              and quantum theories? These are examples of the kinds of
              questions that motivate my studies.
            </p>

            <p>
              For me, doing theoretical physics is not simply a matter of
              collecting interesting ideas. It requires learning the
              mathematics carefully, understanding where equations come
              from, following derivations step by step, and checking whether
              a claim actually follows from the assumptions being made.
              I value the work behind a result as much as the result itself.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="about-side-note">
            <span class="side-note-label">AREAS I KEEP RETURNING TO</span>

            <ul class="topic-list">
              <li>
                <span class="topic-number">01</span>
                <span>
                  <strong>Quantum gravity</strong>
                  <small>Questions about gravity and quantum theory</small>
                </span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="topic-number">02</span>
                <span>
                  <strong>Three-dimensional gravity</strong>
                  <small>Geometric and gauge-theoretic descriptions</small>
                </span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="topic-number">03</span>
                <span>
                  <strong>AdS/CFT and holography</strong>
                  <small>Connections between gravity and quantum field theory</small>
                </span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="topic-number">04</span>
                <span>
                  <strong>High-energy theory</strong>
                  <small>Mathematical structures underlying physical theories</small>
                </span>
              </li>
            </ul>

            <a class="about-text-link" href={`${base}research/`}>
              Explore my research archive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- THE BIGGER QUESTION -->
    <section class="about-philosophy">
      <div class="about-container philosophy-inner">
        <span class="about-eyebrow">03 / THE BIGGER PICTURE</span>

        <blockquote>
          I want to understand the universe as deeply as I can,
          and to remain honest about how much there is still to understand.
        </blockquote>

        <div class="philosophy-copy">
          <p>
            My ambitions are not limited to mastering a particular subject
            or completing a set of academic milestones. I am interested in
            the larger picture: how our different ways of understanding
            the world fit together, where our explanations reach their
            limits, and whether there is a deeper unity beneath the
            theories we currently have.
          </p>

          <p>
            The possibility of a unified description of nature is one of
            the questions that interests me. I do not assume that such a
            theory must exist, or that the universe necessarily has the
            kind of simplicity we might hope to find. I am interested in
            pursuing the question seriously, including the possibility
            that the answer may be more complicated than we expect.
          </p>

          <p>
            This is where physics and philosophy meet for me. Physics gives
            us precise mathematical frameworks and ways to test our ideas.
            Philosophy helps us examine the assumptions, concepts, and
            questions that shape our understanding. Neither removes the
            need for the other kind of care: being precise about what we
            know, questioning what we take for granted, and distinguishing
            a compelling possibility from an established result.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="philosophy-footnote">
          <span class="footnote-line"></span>
          <span>Curiosity is a starting point, not a substitute for evidence.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- DISCIPLINE -->
    <section class="about-section about-discipline">
      <div class="about-container">
        <div class="about-section-heading">
          <span class="about-index">04 / DISCIPLINE</span>
          <h2>Learning to work at the limits of my ability.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="about-two-column discipline-grid">
          <div class="about-prose">
            <p>
              There is another side to the life I want to build: the effort
              of learning difficult things, training hard, and testing my
              physical and mental limits. I do not think of these as
              separate from the person I am trying to become.
            </p>

            <p>
              Research can demand patience with problems that do not yield
              quickly. Learning a difficult subject means accepting that
              understanding takes time, that mistakes are part of the
              process, and that progress is not always immediately visible.
              Training teaches its own lessons about consistency, effort,
              recovery, and the difference between wanting an outcome and
              doing the work required to pursue it.
            </p>

            <p>
              I do not mean that physical training and intellectual work
              are the same thing. They are not. But both ask something
              from you beyond enthusiasm. They ask you to show up, pay
              attention, work through difficulty, and keep improving
              without expecting every session or every day to feel
              extraordinary.
            </p>

            <p>
              I want to become more capable, physically and intellectually,
              while learning to recognise the limits of my current
              understanding. Ambition matters to me, but so does the
              discipline to examine my own work honestly.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="discipline-card">
            <div class="discipline-card-top">
              <span class="discipline-mark">↗</span>
              <span class="side-note-label">A CONTINUING PRACTICE</span>
            </div>

            <div class="discipline-item">
              <span class="discipline-line"></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Study deeply</h3>
                <p>Work towards understanding, rather than familiarity alone.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="discipline-item">
              <span class="discipline-line"></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Train consistently</h3>
                <p>Keep making an effort to develop physical capability.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="discipline-item">
              <span class="discipline-line"></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Question honestly</h3>
                <p>Be willing to revisit an idea when the reasoning does not hold.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="discipline-item">
              <span class="discipline-line"></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Keep learning</h3>
                <p>Leave room to change my mind as I understand more.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- BEYOND RESEARCH -->
    <section class="about-section about-beyond">
      <div class="about-container">
        <div class="about-section-heading">
          <span class="about-index">05 / BEYOND RESEARCH</span>
          <h2>A life should have room for more than one kind of curiosity.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="about-prose about-prose-wide">
          <p>
            Physics occupies a central place in my intellectual life, but
            it is not the only thing I care about. I also want to read
            widely, write about ideas, think about how I see the world,
            and make room for creative work. These interests do not always
            need to support my research or turn into something productive.
            They are worth pursuing in their own right.
          </p>

          <p>
            Reading lets me encounter arguments and perspectives beyond
            my immediate field. Writing gives me a way to work through
            ideas, explain what I think, and discover where my understanding
            is still incomplete. I am interested in recommendations and
            works that leave something to think about, whether they concern
            science, philosophy, literature, or other parts of human life.
          </p>

          <p>
            I also care about photography, painting, and other forms of
            creative expression. They offer ways of noticing and representing
            things that are different from the language of equations and
            formal arguments. I do not want to force every interest into
            a single identity. Some things can be connected; others can
            simply coexist.
          </p>

          <p>
            The aim is not to present a perfectly balanced or finished
            version of myself. It is to leave room for different kinds of
            attention: the precision needed for a calculation, the patience
            needed to learn a skill, the openness needed to read someone
            else's perspective, and the freedom to make something without
            having to justify it as research.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="interest-grid">
          <a class="interest-card" href={`${base}writings/`}>
            <span class="interest-number">01</span>
            <span class="interest-card-content">
              <strong>Writing & ideas</strong>
              <span>Essays, reflections, academic writing, and notes.</span>
            </span>
            <span class="interest-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>

          <a class="interest-card" href={`${base}art/`}>
            <span class="interest-number">02</span>
            <span class="interest-card-content">
              <strong>Photography & art</strong>
              <span>Images, paintings, and creative experiments.</span>
            </span>
            <span class="interest-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>

          <a class="interest-card" href={`${base}media/`}>
            <span class="interest-number">03</span>
            <span class="interest-card-content">
              <strong>Videos & public work</strong>
              <span>Different channels for different subjects and interests.</span>
            </span>
            <span class="interest-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHY THIS WEBSITE EXISTS -->
    <section class="about-section about-website">
      <div class="about-container">
        <div class="about-section-heading">
          <span class="about-index">06 / THIS WEBSITE</span>
          <h2>A record of what I am learning, making, and questioning.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="about-two-column website-grid">
          <div class="about-prose">
            <p>
              I wanted a place of my own where my work could live together
              without everything being reduced to a résumé, a publication
              list, or a social-media profile. This website is intended
              to be that place: a public record of the things I study,
              the ideas I develop, the work I finish, and the questions
              I have not resolved.
            </p>

            <p>
              The research archive is the centre of the site. It is where
              I want to organise research projects, technical notes,
              preprints, academic writings, presentations, and related
              material. I also want to make room for exploratory work,
              unfinished notes, and ideas I eventually decide not to
              pursue. Their status should be clear, so that a working
              draft is not mistaken for a finished result.
            </p>

            <p>
              The other sections provide space for writing, reading,
              recommendations, creative work, and the videos and other
              material I publish. Each has its own purpose. They belong
              together because they are all part of what I spend my time
              thinking about and making, not because they must all be
              about the same subject.
            </p>

            <p>
              I expect the site to change as my work and interests change.
              Some things will become more developed; some will remain
              rough; some may be abandoned. I would rather make that
              process visible than pretend that everything I put here
              represents a final position.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="website-principles">
            <span class="side-note-label">HOW I WANT THIS SPACE TO WORK</span>

            <div class="principle">
              <span class="principle-number">01</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Open</h3>
                <p>Make research notes and other work accessible where possible.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="principle">
              <span class="principle-number">02</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Clear</h3>
                <p>Distinguish published work from drafts, experiments, and unfinished ideas.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="principle">
              <span class="principle-number">03</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Independent</h3>
                <p>Keep a personal space that is not defined by one platform.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="principle">
              <span class="principle-number">04</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Evolving</h3>
                <p>Let the archive grow as my understanding and interests develop.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CLOSING -->
    <section class="about-closing">
      <div class="about-container closing-inner">
        <span class="about-eyebrow">STILL IN PROGRESS</span>

        <h2>
          I have a long way to go.
          <em>That is part of the point.</em>
        </h2>

        <p>
          I am still learning the subjects I care about, still testing my
          abilities, and still working out what kind of person I want to
          become. I do not have a final answer to the questions that
          motivate me. For now, I want to keep studying carefully,
          thinking honestly, making things, and following the questions
          that seem worth my time.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you are here for the physics, the writing, or something
          creative, I hope you find something worth exploring.
        </p>

        <div class="closing-actions">
          <a class="about-button about-button-primary" href={`${base}research/`}>
            Visit the research archive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>

          <a class="about-button about-button-secondary" href={`${base}writings/`}>
            Read my writing
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .about-page {
      --about-ink: #18252e;
      --about-muted: #62717b;
      --about-line: #dce4e8;
      --about-paper: #fbfaf7;
      --about-blue: #dcebf1;
      --about-accent: #b75e3f;
      color: var(--about-ink);
      background: var(--about-paper);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .about-page *,
    .about-page *::before,
    .about-page *::after {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    .about-container {
      width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 48px));
      margin-inline: auto;
    }

    .about-hero {
      padding: 88px 0 26px;
      background:
        radial-gradient(ellipse at 85% 18%, rgba(202, 224, 233, 0.48), transparent 35%),
        var(--about-paper);
    }

    .about-hero-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(290px, 0.8fr);
      align-items: center;
      gap: clamp(42px, 8vw, 110px);
    }

    .about-eyebrow,
    .about-index,
    .side-note-label {
      display: inline-block;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: 0.15em;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .about-eyebrow {
      color: var(--about-accent);
    }

    .about-hero h1 {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 22px 0 24px;
      font-size: clamp(3rem, 6.3vw, 5.65rem);
      font-weight: 580;
      line-height: 0.99;
      letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    }

    .about-hero h1 em,
    .about-closing h2 em {
      color: #507b8d;
      font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      font-weight: 400;
    }

    .about-lead {
      max-width: 640px;
      margin: 0;
      color: #43545e;
      font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.2rem);
      line-height: 1.85;
    }

    .about-hero-note {
      margin: 30px 0 0;
      padding-left: 15px;
      border-left: 2px solid var(--about-accent);
      color: var(--about-muted);
      font-size: 0.91rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .about-identity {
      position: relative;
      display: grid;
      min-height: 400px;
      place-items: center;
      isolation: isolate;
    }

    .identity-orbit {
      position: absolute;
      z-index: -1;
      width: 290px;
      height: 290px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(76, 119, 138, 0.3);
      border-radius: 50%;
    }

    .orbit-one {
      transform: rotate(-24deg) scaleX(0.72);
    }

    .orbit-two {
      width: 340px;
      height: 210px;
      transform: rotate(42deg);
      border-color: rgba(183, 94, 63, 0.32);
    }

    .identity-core {
      display: flex;
      width: 205px;
      height: 205px;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 14px;
      padding: 24px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(76, 119, 138, 0.25);
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: rgba(230, 240, 244, 0.85);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .identity-symbol {
      color: #507b8d;
      font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      font-size: 4.2rem;
      line-height: 1;
    }

    .identity-label {
      max-width: 130px;
      color: #425660;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .identity-note {
      position: absolute;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--about-line);
      border-radius: 30px;
      background: var(--about-paper);
      color: #455761;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
    }

    .identity-note-top {
      top: 58px;
      right: 0;
    }

    .identity-note-bottom {
      bottom: 100px;
      left: 0;
    }

    .identity-dot {
      width: 7px;
      height: 7px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--about-accent);
    }

    .identity-caption {
      position: absolute;
      right: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      left: 0;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .identity-caption span {
      color: var(--about-muted);
      font-size: 0.64rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    }

    .identity-caption p {
      margin: 7px 0 0;
      color: #40545f;
      font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-style: italic;
    }

    .about-hero-footer {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 12px 24px;
      margin-top: 70px;
      padding: 20px 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--about-line);
      color: #697780;
      font-size: 0.66rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    }

    .about-section {
      padding: clamp(72px, 9vw, 116px) 0;
    }

    .about-origin {
      background: #fff;
    }

    .about-section-heading {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, 0.55fr) minmax(0, 1.45fr);
      align-items: start;
      gap: 36px;
      margin-bottom: 44px;
    }

    .about-index {
      padding-top: 12px;
      color: var(--about-accent);
    }

    .about-section-heading h2 {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.35rem);
      font-weight: 550;
      line-height: 1.13;
      letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    }

    .about-prose {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin-left: auto;
    }

    .about-prose p,
    .philosophy-copy p {
      margin: 0 0 22px;
      color: #465761;
      font-size: 1.025rem;
      line-height: 1.95;
    }

    .about-prose p:last-child,
    .philosophy-copy p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .about-physics {
      background: #f0f5f6;
    }

    .about-two-column {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(280px, 0.75fr);
      gap: clamp(42px, 7vw, 88px);
      align-items: start;
    }

    .about-side-note {
      padding: 28px;
      border: 1px solid #d8e2e5;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
    }

    .side-note-label {
      color: #6c7a82;
      font-size: 0.65rem;
    }

    .topic-list {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0;
      margin: 20px 0 24px;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .topic-list li {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 32px 1fr;
      gap: 12px;
      padding: 17px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #dce5e8;
    }

    .topic-number {
      padding-top: 2px;
      color: var(--about-accent);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 750;
    }

    .topic-list strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 5px;
      font-size: 0.93rem;
      font-weight: 650;
    }

    .topic-list small {
      display: block;
      color: var(--about-muted);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .about-text-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      color: #385f70;
      font-size: 0.86rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .about-text-link:hover {
      color: var(--about-accent);
    }

    .about-philosophy {
      padding: clamp(76px, 10vw, 130px) 0;
